---
code: K0015
title: Bad Record Entry
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, record, spread, punning]
description: "Record entry must be 'name: value', 'name:', or '...spread'"
---

Every entry inside a record literal `{ ... }` must be a field assignment (`name: value`), a punned field (`name:`), or a record spread (`...other`).

## Example

This error occurs when a record literal contains a bare identifier without a trailing `:`, a non-identifier key, or an arbitrary expression:

```kura
let width = 100px
let box = { width, height: 50px }

let bad = { "key": 123 }
```

## Solution

Provide a `: value` pair for each field, add a trailing `:` when punning an existing variable, or prefix a record expression with `...` to spread its fields:

```kura
let width = 100px
let defaults = { opacity: 1.0 }
let box = { width:, height: 50px, ...defaults }
```

If you intended to write a block expression rather than a record literal, ensure the first statement inside `{ ... }` is not `name:` (for example, `{ compute(x) }`).
